Q: Redux Toolkit vs Zustand: which is better for global state management in a Next.js e-commerce app? A: <p>This is not how you use reducers in redux. If you read the docs you'll find three main rules for reducers. And the second one is that they &quot;are not allowed to modify the existing state&quot;. And this is exactly what you are doing in your example. Instead you should do something like this:</p>
<pre><code>addToCart: (state, action) =&gt; {
  return ({ cartItems: [...state.cartItems, action.payload] });
},
</code></pre>

